  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full eighteen-song set at the Tractor Tavern in Seattle, Washington, on Tuesday, June 6, 2017 [1][2]. This concert was the second night of a two-day run in the city, following a show at the Showbox the previous evening [2]. The lineup featured a mix of well-known tracks and deep cuts, including \"Rain in Soho,\" \"Harlem Roulette,\" and \"Up the Wolves\" [1]. Notable rarities in the setlist include \"Stench of the Unburied,\" which has only four archived performances, and \"Spent Gladiator,\" a mythic rarity with just two archived shows [1][2]. The band also played \"The Recognition Scene,\" which was the first time it appeared in fifty-one archived shows [1][2]. This recording is the only available capture of the event, documented as an audience recording that runs for one hundred and three minutes [1]. The audio was taped by tungol using a Tascam IM2 connected to an iPhone 5s, which then fed into a Tascam PCM recorder [1]. The file was later transferred and mastered by roffels, who used Izotope for loudness normalization and Audacity for midside decoding and track cuts [1]. As the twenty-third show in the archive’s collection for the band, this performance offers a complete look at their setlist structure during that tour [2]. The recording provides a clear view of the band's dynamic, capturing the full scope of their musical output for that specific night in Seattle [1][2].",
